window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["people-nagumo-miyabi"]=[{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v4_5-p72-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"horikita-manabu nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 3  a passing mention named for the first time in this volume  tachibana says next year s change means nagumo kun s election as student council president  manabu frames the coming school change as something he will need power to combat  tachibana reads it as the nagumo presidency  ak has never heard the name from any first year and infers nagumo is a second year","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v4_5-p72-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: a passing mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.72<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named for the first time in this volume: Tachibana says next year&#x27;s change means Nagumo-kun&#x27;s election as student council president.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Manabu frames the coming school change as something he will need power to combat; Tachibana reads it as the Nagumo presidency.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> AK has never heard the name from any first-year and infers Nagumo is a second-year.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v4_5-p177-1\">→ After: Ch.6: the vice president&#x27;s show<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v4_5-p177-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune ichinose-honami nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 6  the vice president s show the blond player the crowd cheers is nagumo miyabi  a second year class a student and student council vice president who dominates the pool volleyball game  his volleyball spike dominates the game by himself  the girls  high pitched cheers drown out the other matches going on at the same time  kushida names him nagumo senpai from class a  a second year who is really popular with the girls  ichinose adds that he is the current student council vice president  said to take over as president next year  and really smart  every time he shows off  her shoulders tighten slightly at the student council connection  during the student council elections president horikita and nagumo both ran for president  when nagumo was just a first year student  the final decision on ichinose s application came from nagumo  she heard president horikita seemed disappointed in this year s first year students  she models her goal on him   both rose from class b   and says she will become president after him  then adds she was just kidding  she calls his potential limited and his start delayed  he is the reason her shoulders tighten at the student council words  the earring visible on him is a clip on  ichinose says he dresses normally in school  ichinose believes president horikita might be stepping down in october  leaving nagumo next in line","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v4_5-p177-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: the vice president&#x27;s show<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.177–182<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The blond player the crowd cheers is Nagumo Miyabi, a second-year Class A student and student council vice president who dominates the pool volleyball game.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> His volleyball spike dominates the game by himself; the girls&#x27; high-pitched cheers drown out the other matches going on at the same time.<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Kushida names him Nagumo-senpai from Class A, a second year who is really popular with the girls.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Ichinose adds that he is the current student council vice president, said to take over as president next year, and really smart.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Every time he shows off, her shoulders tighten slightly at the student council connection.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> During the student council elections President Horikita and Nagumo both ran for president, when Nagumo was just a first-year student.<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> The final decision on Ichinose&#x27;s application came from Nagumo; she heard President Horikita seemed disappointed in this year&#x27;s first-year students.<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> She models her goal on him — both rose from Class B — and says she will become president after him, then adds she was just kidding.<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She calls his potential limited and his start delayed; he is the reason her shoulders tighten at the student council words.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> The earring visible on him is a clip-on; Ichinose says he dresses normally in school.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Ichinose believes President Horikita might be stepping down in October, leaving Nagumo next in line.<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v4_5-p72-1\">← Before: Ch.3: a passing mention<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v4_5-p185-1\">→ After: Ch.6: a passing mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v4_5-p185-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 6  a passing mention sudou s spike power is measured against nagumo s during the volleyball game","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v4_5-p185-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: a passing mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.185<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sudou&#x27;s spike power is measured against Nagumo&#x27;s during the volleyball game.<\/p><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v4_5-p177-1\">← Before: Ch.6: the vice president&#x27;s show<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v5-p68-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune horikita-manabu nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 5 sec  5  the practice pitch nagumo strolls onto the soccer pitch mid practice and is greeted by kushida by nickname   i see you re on a date   we don t really hold back here  so i think this is a good way to measure our players  strengths  calls her  kikyou chan  and winks before rejoining the game  outclasses both hirata and shibata in the practice game  then scores from midfield    in a different league  horikita refuses to concede the skill   he s just really athletic  that s all  introduced as the candidate to be next student council president  abilities on par with horikita s older brother","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v5-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 sec. 5: The practice pitch<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.68–85<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Nagumo strolls onto the soccer pitch mid-practice and is greeted by Kushida by nickname.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I see you’re on a date.”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“We don’t really hold back here, so I think this is a good way to measure our players’ strengths,”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Calls her “Kikyou-chan” and winks before rejoining the game.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Outclasses both Hirata and Shibata in the practice game, then scores from midfield — “in a different league.”<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Horikita refuses to concede the skill: “He’s just really athletic, that’s all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Introduced as the candidate to be next student council president, abilities on par with Horikita’s older brother.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v5-p79-1\">→ After: Ch.5, Ch.9: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v5-p79-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 5  ch 9  passing mentions second year soccer players take a break  nagumo calls to hirata on the track  horikita and ayanokouji watch the exchange from the stands  shibata chases down nagumo on the anchor leg  ayanokouji s eyes meet the president s instead","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v5-p79-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5, Ch.9: passing mentions<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.79, 187<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Second-year soccer players take a break; Nagumo calls to Hirata on the track.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Horikita and Ayanokouji watch the exchange from the stands.<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Shibata chases down Nagumo on the anchor leg; Ayanokouji’s eyes meet the president’s instead.<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v5-p68-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5: The practice pitch<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v5-p183-1\">→ After: Ch.9 sec. 9: the second-year anchor’s politics<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v5-p183-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-manabu nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 9 sec  9  the second year anchor s politics nagumo runs the second year anchor leg and tells the student council president he will remake the school as a meritocracy   looks like victory is ours this time  president horikita  i would ve liked to run against you directly  if possible   looks like we re going to win in overall points  too  guess this is the dawn of a new era  eh   you re too traditional  and even though you re strict  you re weak  your rules are too generous  and they stop people from getting expelled  all i m going to do is help make this school the ultimate meritocracy  addresses the president by title while taking the second year anchor baton","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v5-p183-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.9 sec. 9: the second-year anchor’s politics<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.183–185<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Nagumo runs the second-year anchor leg and tells the student council president he will remake the school as a meritocracy.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Looks like victory is ours this time, President Horikita. I would’ve liked to run against you directly, if possible.”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Looks like we’re going to win in overall points, too. Guess this is the dawn of a new era, eh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’re too traditional. And even though you’re strict, you’re weak. Your rules are too generous, and they stop people from getting expelled. All I’m going to do is help make this school the ultimate meritocracy,”<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Addresses the president by title while taking the second-year anchor baton.<span class=\"pg\">p.184–185<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v5-p79-1\">← Before: Ch.5, Ch.9: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v6-p14-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"narration spoken","w":"horikita-manabu nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 2  sworn in as student council president second year class a member introduced as the next president  he takes the microphone after horikita manabu s farewell   hello  i m nagumo  second year class a  student council president horikita  i sincerely appreciate the strict yet kind guidance you ve shown me   i d like to express my respect for you  while also emphasizing what an honor it s been to serve alongside the most capable president in this school s history  you ve exhibited the strongest leadership possible   allow me to introduce myself again  my name is nagumo miyabi  and i will be assuming the position of student council president at the tokyo metropolitan advanced nurturing high school  i sincerely look forward to working with all of you  pledges  indefinite officer terms while enrolled  annul october general election  no size cap  open officer intake  majority vote removal   to bring this school into the future  i intend to thoroughly destroy the past  enigmatic during the sports festival  then the picture of politeness   until the reform announcement changes the atmosphere   a revolution is coming  students with real ability will rise to the top  and students without any will fall  i intend to turn this school into a true meritocracy  so please  give me everything you ve got  i look forward to seeing what you can do  glances at horikita while explaining he cannot implement the changes at once as a newly elected president  almost every second year shouts delight  first years do not know the second third year tension behind it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v6-p14-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: sworn in as student council president<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.14–16<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Second-year Class A member introduced as the next president; he takes the microphone after Horikita Manabu’s farewell.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hello. I’m Nagumo, second-year Class A. Student Council President Horikita, I sincerely appreciate the strict yet kind guidance you’ve shown me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’d like to express my respect for you, while also emphasizing what an honor it’s been to serve alongside the most capable president in this school’s history. You’ve exhibited the strongest leadership possible.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Allow me to introduce myself again. My name is Nagumo Miyabi, and I will be assuming the position of student council president at the Tokyo Metropolitan Advanced Nurturing High School. I sincerely look forward to working with…”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Allow me to introduce myself again. My name is Nagumo Miyabi, and I will be assuming the position of student council president at the Tokyo Metropolitan Advanced Nurturing High School. I sincerely look forward to working with all of you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Pledges: indefinite officer terms while enrolled; annul October general election; no size cap; open officer intake; majority-vote removal.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To bring this school into the future, I intend to thoroughly destroy the past.”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Enigmatic during the sports festival, then the picture of politeness — until the reform announcement changes the atmosphere.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A revolution is coming. Students with real ability will rise to the top, and students without any will fall. I intend to turn this school into a true meritocracy, so please, give me everything you’ve got. I look forward to seeing what you can do.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Glances at Horikita while explaining he cannot implement the changes at once as a newly elected president.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> Almost every second-year shouts delight; first years do not know the second/third-year tension behind it.<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v6-p70-1\">→ After: Ch.4: contrasted with Ryuuen’s violence<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v6-p70-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"","w":"horikita-manabu ryuuen-kakeru nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 4  contrasted with ryuuen s violence named as current president in the same contrast with former president horikita  paired with him as the authority style ryuuen wields violence against instead  ryuuen  i will not yield to authority  even if the school tries to expel me    their style is not his  no dialogue or action from nagumo on these pages","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v6-p70-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: contrasted with Ryuuen’s violence<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.70<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as current president in the same contrast with former-president Horikita.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Paired with him as the authority style Ryuuen wields violence against instead.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Ryuuen: I will not yield to authority. Even if the school tries to expel me… — their style is not his.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No dialogue or action from Nagumo on these pages.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v6-p14-1\">← Before: Ch.2: sworn in as student council president<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v7-p87-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"","w":"horikita-manabu ichinose-honami katsuragi-kouhei ayanokouji-kiyotaka nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 3  named through manabu the subject of manabu s dorm room warning   failed successor  council hijacker  coming expulsions  second year class a  current student council president  ayanokoji only exchanged pleasantries at the sports festival  ideologies differed from manabu s  almost all second year students under his sway   already won over the entire school  worked behind manabu to contact ichinose and force her onto the council  the successor who went wrong  the man manabu watches  the first year he snatched onto the council  the other applicant manabu refused to protect them both  warned about him  still declines the student council game","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v7-p87-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: named through Manabu<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.87–89<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The subject of Manabu’s dorm-room warning — failed successor, council hijacker, coming expulsions.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Second-year Class A, current student council president; Ayanokōji only exchanged pleasantries at the sports festival.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ideologies differed from Manabu’s; almost all second-year students under his sway; “already won over the entire school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Worked behind Manabu to contact Ichinose and force her onto the council.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> The successor who went wrong; the man Manabu watches.<span class=\"pg\">p.87–89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The first-year he snatched onto the council.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The other applicant Manabu refused to protect them both.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Warned about him; still declines the student-council game.<span class=\"pg\">p.87–89<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v7_5-p86-1","v":"y1v7.5","y":1,"o":9,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-manabu horikita-suzune nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 4  the target of the debt named as the new student council president whose way horikita manabu wants stopped   nagumo s just tryin  to make this shitty  boring ass school into something fun  from the sound of it    speaker is ryuuen  nagumo does not speak in ch4  the debt ayanokoji owes is to stop him  manabu prepared student council briefs  if suzune joins the student council  manabu would cooperate   a nagumo adjacent lever  seventeen second year expulsions already  involved in over half the cases per exit interviews","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v7_5-p86-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: the target of the debt<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7.5 · p.86–92<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as the new student council president whose way Horikita Manabu wants stopped.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Nagumo’s just tryin’ to make this shitty, boring-ass school into something fun, from the sound of it.” — speaker is Ryuuen; Nagumo does not speak in ch4.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> The debt Ayanokōji owes is to stop him; Manabu prepared student-council briefs.<span class=\"pg\">p.86–92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> If Suzune joins the student council, Manabu would cooperate — a Nagumo-adjacent lever.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Seventeen second-year expulsions already; involved in over half the cases per exit interviews.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v7_5-p123-1\">→ After: Ch.5: the arm-grab and the online-game tease<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v7_5-p123-1","v":"y1v7.5","y":1,"o":9,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-manabu hirata-yousuke ichinose-honami nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 5  the arm grab and the online game tease interrupts the double date outside the theater with kiriyama  mizowaki  tonokawa and ichinose  grabs ayanokoji s arm   you re the student horikita senpai s been so fixated on  i m just following the rumors  is all   former student council president  after he graduates  i have a whole year at this school  won t you play with me   i imagine that you first years have had some shitty  boring tests so far  what if we had a special test based on a popular online game   sorry for pushing in on your date  see ya around  targets him because manabu talks to him  the mystery second year is about stopping him  rival  manabu s influence on ayanokoji  doesn t sit well  soccer club under him  people who butted heads quit and dropped out  walks with his entourage  gentle smile at ayanokoji  grabs ayanokoji s arm without letting go while smiling amiably","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v7_5-p123-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5: the arm-grab and the online-game tease<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7.5 · p.123–126, 131–132, 145, 149, 151–153<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Interrupts the double date outside the theater with Kiriyama, Mizowaki, Tonokawa and Ichinose; grabs Ayanokōji’s arm.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’re the student Horikita-senpai’s been so fixated on. I’m just following the rumors, is all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Former student council president. After he graduates, I have a whole year at this school. Won’t you play with me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I imagine that you first years have had some shitty, boring tests so far… What if we had a special test based on a popular online game?”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry for pushing in on your date. See ya around.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Targets him because Manabu talks to him; the mystery second year is about stopping him.<span class=\"pg\">p.123–126, 145, 151–153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Rival; Manabu’s influence on Ayanokōji “doesn’t sit well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.125, 151–153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Soccer club under him; people who butted heads quit and dropped out.<span class=\"pg\">p.123–126, 131–132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Walks with his entourage; gentle smile at Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Grabs Ayanokōji’s arm without letting go while smiling amiably.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v7_5-p86-1\">← Before: Ch.4: the target of the debt<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v7_5-p149-1\">→ After: Ch.5: named in the threat list<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v7_5-p149-1","v":"y1v7.5","y":1,"o":9,"k":"","w":"nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 5  named in the threat list named once in ayanokoji s honeypot math as a threat who would not crumble karuizawa now  passing mention   if ryuuen  or sakayanagi  or even someone like nagumo approached her  she wouldn t crumble  passing mention only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v7_5-p149-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5: named in the threat list<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7.5 · p.149<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once in Ayanokōji’s honeypot math as a threat who would not crumble Karuizawa now.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: “If Ryuuen, or Sakayanagi, or even someone like Nagumo approached her, she wouldn’t crumble.”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only.<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v7_5-p123-1\">← Before: Ch.5: the arm-grab and the online-game tease<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v7_5-p155-1\">→ After: Ch.6: the enemy Kiriyama describes<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v7_5-p155-1","v":"y1v7.5","y":1,"o":9,"k":"","w":"kiriyama-ikuto ayanokouji-kiyotaka nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 6  the enemy kiriyama describes discussed throughout the kiriyama meet  not present  passing mention  kiriyama never agreed with nagumo  nagumo s reform pitch of promoting capable students regardless of class  passing mention only  passing mention  almost all second years under nagumo  dissatisfied but not enough votes  persons of interest list starts third semester  anyone on his bad side expelled across the board  passing mention only  passing mention  ayanokoji s risk model   dirty play could get people expelled  sudou ishizaki fight as example  passing mention only  the regime kiriyama infiltrates and wants removed from office  already on the radar after the relay  ayanokoji weighs pretending the relay was a fluke","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v7_5-p155-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: the enemy Kiriyama describes<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7.5 · p.155–159, 161–162<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Discussed throughout the Kiriyama meet; not present.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kiriyama-ikuto.html\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: Kiriyama never agreed with Nagumo; Nagumo’s reform pitch of promoting capable students regardless of class.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: almost all second-years under Nagumo; dissatisfied but not enough votes; persons-of-interest list starts third semester; anyone on his bad side expelled across the board.<span class=\"pg\">p.156–158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only.<span class=\"pg\">p.156–158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: Ayanokōji’s risk model — dirty play could get people expelled (Sudou/Ishizaki fight as example).<span class=\"pg\">p.161–162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only.<span class=\"pg\">p.161–162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> The regime Kiriyama infiltrates and wants removed from office.<span class=\"pg\">p.155–159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Already on the radar after the relay; Ayanokōji weighs pretending the relay was a fluke.<span class=\"pg\">p.157–162<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v7_5-p149-1\">← Before: Ch.5: named in the threat list<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p10-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"","w":"horikita-manabu nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 1  named as the bulldozer named in manabu s graduation soliloquy as the one who took direct action to clear him from the path  passing mention   nagumo miyabi continues to take direct action against me     perhaps  a bulldozer  is the description that fits him best  passing mention only  pressed manabu for three years  manabu had given up responding before graduation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p10-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.1: named as the bulldozer<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.10<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in Manabu’s graduation soliloquy as the one who took direct action to clear him from the path.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: “Nagumo Miyabi continues to take direct action against me” — “Perhaps ‘a bulldozer’ is the description that fits him best.”<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Pressed Manabu for three years; Manabu had given up responding before graduation.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p11-1\">→ After: Ch.2: named as the grade-level thread to watch<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p11-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 2  named as the grade level thread to watch not on the bus or in the gym  named once in ayanokoji s protection planning as the exam opens  passing mention  given the rare chance for grade levels to intermingle  ayanokoji resolves to keep an eye on nagumo s movements  passing mention only  outside thread ayanokoji flags while listing who he will and will not protect","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p11-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: named as the grade-level thread to watch<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.11–43<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Not on the bus or in the gym; named once in Ayanokōji’s protection planning as the exam opens.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: given the rare chance for grade levels to intermingle, Ayanokōji resolves to keep an eye on Nagumo’s movements.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Outside thread Ayanokōji flags while listing who he will and will not protect.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p10-1\">← Before: Ch.1: named as the bulldozer<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p52-1\">→ After: Ch.2: the early draft, the duel, and Kōenji’s bust<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p52-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-manabu fujimaki kouenji-rokusuke yukimura-teruhiko ayanokouji-kiyotaka nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 2  the early draft  the duel  and koenji s bust after first year small groups finish  nagumo moves the large group draft forward and then presses ayanokoji s delayed group for a representative   how about we form a large group right now   should we have a draft pick system  brief private talk with the former president  then the public challenge   fujimaki interrupts  but nagumo forces the average score duel with anti collateral conditions   how about which of us can get the most students expelled   how about which group can earn the higher average score  taunts fujimaki as third year class a s number two and invites him to be the opponent instead of horikita  exposes koenji s twenty million point class a purchase plan  warns the second  and third years off dealing with him  and says he will report pre graduation point purchases to the school  deduces the delayed groups from the draft timing  orders the representative chosen now  dismisses the group once yukimura volunteers  reads group composition from a one second delay in the rock paper scissors circle   ayanokoji admits the attempt to hide the weakness failed  calls him out after the draft  ayanokoji notes nagumo may be watching at every meal  top dog of second year class a  second years wear worshipful looks   rival  hated enemy  deeply respected","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p52-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: the early draft, the duel, and Kōenji’s bust<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.52–68<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After first-year small groups finish, Nagumo moves the large-group draft forward and then presses Ayanokōji’s delayed group for a representative.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"fujimaki.html\">Fujimaki<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“How about we form a large group right now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Should we have a draft-pick system?”<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“How about which of us can get the most students expelled?”<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Brief private talk with the former president; then the public challenge — Fujimaki interrupts, but Nagumo forces the average-score duel with anti-collateral conditions.<span class=\"pg\">p.53, 57–60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “how about which group can earn the higher average score?”<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Fujimaki<\/b> Taunts Fujimaki as third-year Class A’s number two and invites him to be the opponent instead of Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.57–58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Exposes Kōenji’s twenty-million-point Class A purchase plan, warns the second- and third-years off dealing with him, and says he will report pre-graduation point purchases to the school.<span class=\"pg\">p.64–67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Deduces the delayed groups from the draft timing; orders the representative chosen now; dismisses the group once Yukimura volunteers.<span class=\"pg\">p.61–68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Reads group composition from a one-second delay in the rock-paper-scissors circle — Ayanokōji admits the attempt to hide the weakness failed.<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Calls him out after the draft; Ayanokōji notes Nagumo may be watching at every meal.<span class=\"pg\">p.52, 61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Top dog of second-year Class A; second-years wear worshipful looks — rival, hated enemy, deeply respected.<span class=\"pg\">p.46–47, 57–58<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p11-1\">← Before: Ch.2: named as the grade-level thread to watch<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p55-1\">→ After: Ch.2–9: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p55-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"","w":"nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 2 9  passing mentions named across the third year contest and post exam pages without individual rows beyond his cited scenes  identified as the student kiriyama served under as vice president  demoted after losing to nagumo  tachibana s account centres on how second years  particularly nagumo  operate","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p55-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2–9: passing mentions<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.55–56, 72, 90, 116–117, 144, 159, 200–201<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named across the third-year contest and post-exam pages without individual rows beyond his cited scenes.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Identified as the student Kiriyama served under as vice president, demoted after losing to Nagumo.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Tachibana’s account centres on how second-years, particularly Nagumo, operate.<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p52-1\">← Before: Ch.2: the early draft, the duel, and Kōenji’s bust<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p84-1\">→ After: Ch.3: breakfast order, the card visit, the marked deck<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p84-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka ishikura kiriyama-ikuto nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 3  breakfast order  the card visit  the marked deck at the outdoor breakfast as first years accept the rotation  later invades group six s dorm with kiriyama  tsunoda and ishikura for old maid stakes on breakfast duty   yeah  i ve got no objections  i d like to start with the first years   i came to check on you since we re in the same group  can i come in   let s bet on that  if  for example  you lose constantly  you ll be on meal duty until the end of camp   why don t you join the student council  kouenji  i d love to have someone as interesting as you aboard   you must be glad  ayanokouji  looks like you escaped  invites koenji to the student council  takes his foreseen outcome question seriously enough to answer  then shuffles away amiable when koenji declines all of it  never looks at him until he beckons him in for game five  the last two card offer is a marked joker trap ayanokoji walks past by picking the winner  banter about rooms  soccer vs council  and horikita  ishikura brushes the  might get along just fine  line and leaves abruptly  vp finishes second in the early rounds  nagumo s third place finish in round three is played as bad luck  predicts outcomes in a chance game  holds a sealed box deck he first dealt  the notch on the joker  and still loses the last pick without the marked card being exposed   i d like to leave the first years with three losses  but i m also okay with four    the whole night is a controlled test  not a party","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p84-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: breakfast order, the card visit, the marked deck<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.84–109<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At the outdoor breakfast as first-years accept the rotation; later invades group six’s dorm with Kiriyama, Tsunoda and Ishikura for Old Maid stakes on breakfast duty.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"ishikura.html\">Ishikura<\/a> · <a href=\"kiriyama-ikuto.html\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yeah. I’ve got no objections. I’d like to start with the first-years.”<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I came to check on you since we’re in the same group. Can I come in?”<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Let’s bet on that. If, for example, you lose constantly, you’ll be on meal duty until the end of camp.”<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why don’t you join the student council, Kouenji? I’d love to have someone as interesting as you aboard.”<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You must be glad, Ayanokouji. Looks like you escaped.”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Invites Kōenji to the student council, takes his foreseen-outcome question seriously enough to answer, then shuffles away amiable when Kōenji declines all of it.<span class=\"pg\">p.98, 105–106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Never looks at him until he beckons him in for game five; the last two-card offer is a marked-joker trap Ayanokōji walks past by picking the winner.<span class=\"pg\">p.100, 104, 107–108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishikura<\/b> Banter about rooms, soccer vs council, and Horikita; Ishikura brushes the “might get along just fine” line and leaves abruptly.<span class=\"pg\">p.96–109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> VP finishes second in the early rounds; Nagumo’s third-place finish in round three is played as bad luck.<span class=\"pg\">p.100–103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Predicts outcomes in a chance game, holds a sealed-box deck he first dealt (the notch on the joker), and still loses the last pick without the marked card being exposed.<span class=\"pg\">p.105–108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> “I’d like to leave the first-years with three losses. But I’m also okay with four” — the whole night is a controlled test, not a party.<span class=\"pg\">p.104, 106–109<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p55-1\">← Before: Ch.2–9: passing mentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p118-1\">→ After: Ch.4: the open offer from the sidelines<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p118-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"spoken","w":"ishikura horikita-manabu kiriyama-ikuto nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 4  the open offer from the sidelines watches kiriyama s confrontation from the sidelines and applauds ishikura s handling   excellent  ishikura senpai  you really got a handle on things  didn t you   the only reason you haven t been able to rise to class a is because there s a genius like horikita manabu in your way  i know you ve fought the good fight for three years  there s a 312 point difference between classes a and b right now   it doesn t matter if he s the representative or not  there are many    ways to crush horikita  said with a laugh  lays out class a and horikita removal plans in front of everyone  gets  i can t trust you  for it  names manabu as the blocker  claims many ways to crush him whether or not he is representative  kiriyama s coaching is the occasion  nagumo watches without intervening until after  guileless or performed show of plans   ayanokoji doubts it was the former  312 point gap between classes a and b at the time of the offer","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p118-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: the open offer from the sidelines<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.118–119<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Watches Kiriyama’s confrontation from the sidelines and applauds Ishikura’s handling.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ishikura.html\">Ishikura<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"kiriyama-ikuto.html\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Excellent, Ishikura-senpai. You really got a handle on things, didn’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“The only reason you haven’t been able to rise to Class A is because there’s a genius like Horikita Manabu in your way. I know you’ve fought the good fight for three years. There’s a 312-point difference between Classes A and B…”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It doesn’t matter if he’s the representative or not. There are many” — ways to crush Horikita, said with a laugh.<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The only reason you haven’t been able to rise to Class A is because there’s a genius like Horikita Manabu in your way. I know you’ve fought the good fight for three years. There’s a 312-point difference between Classes A and B right now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishikura<\/b> Lays out Class A and Horikita-removal plans in front of everyone; gets “I can’t trust you” for it.<span class=\"pg\">p.118–119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Names Manabu as the blocker; claims many ways to crush him whether or not he is representative.<span class=\"pg\">p.118–119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> Kiriyama’s coaching is the occasion; Nagumo watches without intervening until after.<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Guileless-or-performed show of plans — Ayanokōji doubts it was the former.<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Numbers<\/span> 312-point gap between Classes A and B at the time of the offer.<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p84-1\">← Before: Ch.3: breakfast order, the card visit, the marked deck<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p146-1\">→ After: Ch.4: named in the corridor assessment<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p146-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"","w":"horikita-manabu ayanokouji-kiyotaka nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 4  named in the corridor assessment not on the page  named throughout manabu s corridor brief to ayanokoji  passing mention in manabu s assessment  nagumo s public average score challenge  underhanded methods  unusually high second year expulsion rate  never broken a promise  passing mention only  the two year student council history is why manabu trusts the no third parties claim  ayanokoji withholds his own nagumo concerns while taking the brief  manabu s group is mostly class a including first years   strong chance to win the test  that is why nagumo s inaction reads as anxiety fuel","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p146-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: named in the corridor assessment<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.146<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Not on the page; named throughout Manabu’s corridor brief to Ayanokōji.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention in Manabu’s assessment: Nagumo’s public average-score challenge, underhanded methods, unusually high second-year expulsion rate, never broken a promise.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> The two-year student-council history is why Manabu trusts the no-third-parties claim.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Ayanokōji withholds his own Nagumo concerns while taking the brief.<span class=\"pg\">p.145–146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Manabu’s group is mostly Class A including first-years — strong chance to win the test; that is why Nagumo’s inaction reads as anxiety fuel.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p118-1\">← Before: Ch.4: the open offer from the sidelines<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p150-1\">→ After: Ch.5: named in the hanging-around rumor<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p150-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"","w":"ichinose-honami nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 5  named in the hanging around rumor not on the page  named when a class a girl raises the student council president rumor  rumor named   people say they see you hanging around with nagumo senpai a lot  just the two of you  ichinose s answer  council work only  not on his radar  no one she likes now  confirmed she worked a lot with him after joining the student council   the grain of truth under the dating rumor","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p150-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5: named in the hanging-around rumor<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.150<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Not on the page; named when a Class A girl raises the student-council-president rumor.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Rumor named: “People say they see you hanging around with Nagumo-senpai a lot, just the two of you…”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Ichinose’s answer: council work only, not on his radar, no one she likes now.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Confirmed she worked a lot with him after joining the student council — the grain of truth under the dating rumor.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p146-1\">← Before: Ch.4: named in the corridor assessment<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p165-1\">→ After: Ch.6 half 1: named only as the group force<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p165-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"","w":"nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 6 half 1  named only as the group force not on the page in half 1  the ryuuen groups context sits under nagumo s exam design  half 2 develops it  no half 1 dialogue or action   half 2 asahina interview carries his picture","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p165-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 half 1: named only as the group force<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.165<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Not on the page in half 1; the Ryuuen-groups context sits under Nagumo’s exam design (half 2 develops it).<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> No half 1 dialogue or action — half 2 Asahina interview carries his picture.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p150-1\">← Before: Ch.5: named in the hanging-around rumor<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p173-1\">→ After: Ch.6 half 2: the picture Asahina draws<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p173-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"","w":"asahina-nazuna horikita-manabu ayanokouji-kiyotaka ishikura nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 6 half 2  the picture asahina draws not on the page  built entirely through ayanokoji s plan and asahina s interview  target of the probe  true intentions toward horikita s brother  asahina  respects horikita senpai  made him a goal  jealous of missing the relay challenge  second years shared bus exam info at his urging  four classes on the way to allies  girls  large group adjusted with members miyabi could count on  tachibana s group has the secretary  asahina  always sticks to his word  no dirty tricks   whoever cares too much is the one who loses  the source of the fair square   care too much picture  deep classmate relationship named  the rival frame   goal  jealousy  and the girls  group irrelevance to their fight  the one probing  reads clues that disappear as a unique strategy vs sakayanagi and ryuuen   ishikura senpai  named as the third year his group met   not assigned  see volume note  public promise of fair square plus shadow manufacturing under investigation   feint or real still open","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p173-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 half 2: the picture Asahina draws<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.173–181<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Not on the page; built entirely through Ayanokōji’s plan and Asahina’s interview.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"asahina-nazuna.html\">Asahina Nazuna<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"ishikura.html\">Ishikura<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Target of the probe: true intentions toward Horikita’s brother.<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Asahina: respects Horikita-senpai, made him a goal, jealous of missing the relay challenge.<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Second-years shared bus exam info at his urging; four classes on the way to allies.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Girls’ large group adjusted with members Miyabi could count on; Tachibana’s group has the secretary.<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Asahina: always sticks to his word, no dirty tricks; “whoever cares too much is the one who loses.”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Asahina Nazuna<\/b> The source of the fair-square / care-too-much picture; deep classmate relationship named.<span class=\"pg\">p.176–181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> The rival frame — goal, jealousy, and the girls’ group irrelevance to their fight.<span class=\"pg\">p.176, 180–181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The one probing; reads clues-that-disappear as a unique strategy vs Sakayanagi and Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.173–181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishikura<\/b> “Ishikura-senpai” named as the third-year his group met — not assigned (see volume note).<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Public promise of fair square plus shadow-manufacturing under investigation — feint or real still open.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p165-1\">← Before: Ch.6 half 1: named only as the group force<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p207-1\">→ After: Ch.7: the abstain demand and the name play<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p207-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-manabu ryuuen-kakeru hashimoto-masayoshi ayanokouji-kiyotaka sakayanagi-arisu ichinose-honami nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 7  the abstain demand and the name play interrupts the hashimoto ryuuen meeting with manabu  demands manabu abstain  uses ayanokoji s name on hashimoto   what s up  first years  having a secret meeting at a time like this  huh   i ve heard you re quite the delinquent  your name s ryuuen  right  i m going to have a little chat with horikita senpai  but you should come along   wow  you re confident  not scared of me  ryuuen   heh   i don t dislike people like you   hey  how about you join this wager  as a third party  which group do you think will place higher in today s special exam  mine  or horikita senpai s  how about ten thousand points a head  no matter which side you bet on  i ll pay up if you re right on the money  if you re wrong  though  you gotta pay up   ten thousand is  that kind of money  huh  you re in class d  meaning you re always short on cash  right  can t hurt to earn a little more   hahaha  you re a funny guy  ryuuen  talk about a ballsy joke   hey  you  first year  you think ryuuen can pay that much   if we had our phones  we could check  i wouldn t mind playing along then  too bad   horikita senpai  please abstain from taking the exam tomorrow   that s right   actually  i m being quite serious   it s for your own sake  senpai   sorry  being able to see too far into the future is a curse  anyway  if you don t kindly abstain tomorrow  senpai  you ll regret it  what i m saying is that i m trying to help you  i could just put the hurt on you without warning  but that would just be heartless  wouldn t it   i understand  the rules of our contest are that we have to fight fair and square  without involving any third parties   yes  because abstaining will allow you to get through this with the least amount of damage  senpai  are you aware of the strategic groundwork that i ve laid  no  you aren t  are you  there isn t a single student at this school who can read my thoughts   ah  that s right  if i recall  he s in the same group as that first year  ayanokouji kiyotaka   what do you think  hashimoto  about ayanokouji   i know  right  but horikita senpai here seems to value ayanokouji over all other first years   see  horikita senpai prizes ayanokouji above even sakayanagi  even ryuuen  even ichinose  since you re in the same group as him  i thought you might have noticed something   why is that  senpai  please  i think it s about time you tell me the reason   sorry  senpai  i suppose you re right  my bad  hashimoto  that was a little joke  abstain demand  fair square contest frame   strategic groundwork  name drops ayanokoji at manabu  wager offer  million counter laughed off  told he is not really fit for the student council  pulls him into the corridor triangle  uses him for the ayanokoji value test  emphasized by name as manabu s prized first year above sakayanagi  ryuuen  ichinose  named in the prized first year ranking  same ranking list  playful menace  seeing too far into the future called a curse  serious abstain under the joke  walks out on ryuuen s million  win tomorrow with groundwork laid   least damage path for manabu is abstention","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p207-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7: the abstain demand and the name play<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.207–211<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Interrupts the Hashimoto–Ryuuen meeting with Manabu; demands Manabu abstain; uses Ayanokōji’s name on Hashimoto.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“What’s up, first-years? Having a secret meeting at a time like this, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’ve heard you’re quite the delinquent. Your name’s Ryuuen, right? I’m going to have a little chat with Horikita-senpai, but you should come along.”<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Wow, you’re confident. Not scared of me, Ryuuen?”<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>28 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Heh.”<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t dislike people like you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, how about you join this wager, as a third party? Which group do you think will place higher in today’s special exam, mine, or Horikita-senpai’s? How about ten thousand points a head? No matter which side you bet on, I’ll pay up if you’re right on the money. If you’re wrong, though, you gotta pay up.”<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ten thousand is ‘that kind of money’, huh? You’re in Class D, meaning you’re always short on cash, right? Can’t hurt to earn a little more.”<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hahaha! You’re a funny guy, Ryuuen. Talk about a ballsy joke.”<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, you. First-year. You think Ryuuen can pay that much?”<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If we had our phones, we could check. I wouldn’t mind playing along then. Too bad.”<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita-senpai. Please abstain from taking the exam tomorrow”<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s right.”<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Actually, I’m being quite serious.”<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s for your own sake, senpai.”<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry. Being able to see too far into the future is a curse. Anyway, if you don’t kindly abstain tomorrow, senpai, you’ll regret it. What I’m saying is that I’m trying to help you. I could just put the hurt on you without warning, but that would just be heartless, wouldn’t it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand. The rules of our contest are that we have to fight fair and square, without involving any third parties.”<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. Because abstaining will allow you to get through this with the least amount of damage, senpai. Are you aware of the strategic groundwork that I’ve laid? No, you aren’t, are you? There isn’t a single student at this school who can read my thoughts.”<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, that’s right. If I recall, he’s in the same group as that first-year. Ayanokouji Kiyotaka.”<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What do you think, Hashimoto? About Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know, right? But Horikita-senpai here seems to value Ayanokouji over all other first-years.”<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “See, Horikita-senpai prizes Ayanokouji above even Sakayanagi, even Ryuuen, even Ichinose. Since you’re in the same group as him, I thought you might have noticed something.”<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why is that, senpai? Please, I think it’s about time you tell me the reason.”<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry, senpai. I suppose you’re right. My bad, Hashimoto. That was a little joke.”<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Abstain demand; fair-square contest frame; “strategic groundwork”; name-drops Ayanokōji at Manabu.<span class=\"pg\">p.207–211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Wager offer; million counter laughed off; told he is not really fit for the student council.<span class=\"pg\">p.208–209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Pulls him into the corridor triangle; uses him for the Ayanokōji-value test.<span class=\"pg\">p.207–211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Emphasized by name as Manabu’s prized first-year above Sakayanagi, Ryuuen, Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Named in the prized-first-year ranking.<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Same ranking list.<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Playful menace; seeing too far into the future called a curse; serious abstain under the joke; walks out on Ryuuen’s million.<span class=\"pg\">p.208–211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Win tomorrow with groundwork laid — least damage path for Manabu is abstention.<span class=\"pg\">p.209–210<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p173-1\">← Before: Ch.6 half 2: the picture Asahina draws<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p227-1\">→ After: Ch.9 half 1: second place with a smile<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p227-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"","w":"horikita-manabu hashimoto-masayoshi nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 9 half 1  second place with a smile their large group announced second  nagumo smiles beside ayanokoji with no sign of upset  manabu s group first  nagumo s second   the smile is the tell that the loss was the plan  overnight interest in ryuuen still in hashimoto s head  prior context carried into the day  not the look of a man who lost after throwing the gauntlet   the pov reads concoction  not defeat  no direct speech in half 1 after the announcements begin","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p227-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.9 half 1: second place with a smile<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.227–228<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Their large group announced second; Nagumo smiles beside Ayanokōji with no sign of upset.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Manabu’s group first; Nagumo’s second — the smile is the tell that the loss was the plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Overnight interest in Ryuuen still in Hashimoto’s head (prior context carried into the day).<span class=\"pg\">p.220–221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Not the look of a man who lost after throwing the gauntlet — the POV reads concoction, not defeat.<span class=\"pg\">p.227–228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> No direct speech in half 1 after the announcements begin.<span class=\"pg\">p.227–228<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p207-1\">← Before: Ch.7: the abstain demand and the name play<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p229-1\">→ After: Ch.9 half 2: the blind spot<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p229-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-manabu tachibana-akane fujimaki ishikura ikari-momoko nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 9 half 2  the blind spot loud congratulations to horikita senpai  runs the girls  trap to tachibana s naming  the gym floor victory lap and the xp monologue   you ve earned first place  congratulations are in order  horikita senpai  just as i d expect from you  said nagumo  speaking loudly   it sure seems that way  but they ve only just started announcing the results  haven t they   yes  they have nothing to do with the fight between horikita senpai and i  that s right  at all   come now  senpai  we re still in the middle of the results  please calm down  this has nothing to do with you anyway  fujimaki senpai  does it  the only thing that s happening is that a class b student will be expelled  if anything  this means you ll pull even further ahead of your rivals  right   ikari senpai  i m sure everyone is wondering just who in the world will be expelled alongside you   ah  such beautiful friendship  or perhaps i should call it love  anyway  congratulations to you  horikita senpai  once again  please allow me to pay you my compliments  i ve lost   it was a truly fantastic strategy  no  perhaps i should say that it was a strategy that went well beyond what is expected  there is not a single person here who can read my intentions  and that includes you  horikita senpai   please  enlighten me  tachibana senpai  how does it feel to have served on the student council  to have been on verge of graduating from class a  only to then be expelled  and horikita senpai  how do you feel right now  i m sure you must be positively filled with feelings of frustration  the likes of which you ve never felt before  hmm   because i can t imagine you ever being expelled  even if i tried such a method on you  senpai  i was terrified you d counter me with some method i couldn t anticipate  but more importantly  i ve never actually wanted you to be expelled  horikita senpai  if anything  if you got expelled  then we wouldn t be able to see each other  would we  that s why  of all the many possible targets  i went after tachibana senpai  i wanted to see your face when i made her disappear   trust is an awful lot like experience points in a game  he said   the more you accumulate  the more you increase your worth  i think that the ultimate form of this is family  if you ran into a stranger when you were out and about at night  you d be cautious  but if that person happened to be family  then you d drop your guard  it s like that  horikita senpai  though i   i m glad to hear that  this was  after all  nothing more than a warmup  replied nagumo   i m fine with getting people expelled  if i have to  that s the way this school operates  congratulates him loudly  admits never wanting him expelled so they can keep facing each other  the trust discarded as game xp  calls her over for the reveal  the target chosen over manabu to watch his face  enigmatic wording draws fujimaki s stern face  then the  nothing to do with me  denial under the shout down  quiet class b observer beside him  the collusion and the twenty million advance read by the pov  her naming of tachibana is the trap s firing pin  trap set without the school realizing it  class b representative  large group held low  nagumo paid twenty million private points up front so class b would cooperate  forces the lifeline spend  keeps the a b gap from widening while class a burns cash   warmup  for what comes next","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p229-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.9 half 2: the blind spot<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.229–240<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Loud congratulations to Horikita-senpai; runs the girls’ trap to Tachibana’s naming; the gym-floor victory lap and the XP monologue.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"tachibana-akane.html\">Tachibana Akane<\/a> · <a href=\"fujimaki.html\">Fujimaki<\/a> · <a href=\"ishikura.html\">Ishikura<\/a> · <a href=\"ikari-momoko.html\">Ikari Momoko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’ve earned first place. Congratulations are in order, Horikita-senpai. Just as I’d expect from you,” said Nagumo, speaking loudly.<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It sure seems that way. But they’ve only just started announcing the results, haven’t they?”<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yes. They have nothing to do with the fight between Horikita-senpai and I, that’s right. At all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Come now, senpai, we’re still in the middle of the results. Please calm down. This has nothing to do with you anyway, Fujimaki-senpai. Does it? The only thing that’s happening is that a Class B student will be expelled. If anything, this means you’ll pull even further ahead of your rivals, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ikari-senpai. I’m sure everyone is wondering just who in the world will be expelled alongside you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, such beautiful friendship. Or perhaps I should call it love? Anyway, congratulations to you, Horikita-senpai. Once again, please allow me to pay you my compliments. I’ve lost.”<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It was a truly fantastic strategy. No, perhaps I should say that it was a strategy that went well beyond what is expected. There is not a single person here who can read my intentions, and that includes you, Horikita-senpai,”<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Please, enlighten me, Tachibana-senpai. How does it feel to have served on the student council, to have been on verge of graduating from Class A, only to then be expelled? And Horikita-senpai, how do you feel right now? I’m sure you must be positively filled with feelings of frustration, the likes of which you’ve never felt before. Hmm?”<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because I can’t imagine you ever being expelled, even if I tried such a method on you, senpai. I was terrified you’d counter me with some method I couldn’t anticipate. But more importantly, I’ve never actually wanted you to be expelled, Horikita-senpai. If anything, if you got expelled, then we wouldn’t be able to see each other, would we? That’s why, of all the many possible targets, I went after Tachibana-senpai. I wanted to see your face when I made her disappear,”<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Trust is an awful lot like experience points in a game,” he said. “The more you accumulate, the more you increase your worth. I think that the ultimate form of this is family. If you ran into a stranger when you were out and about at night, you’d be cautious. But if that person happened to be family, then you’d drop your guard. It’s like that, Horikita-senpai. Though I”<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m glad to hear that. This was, after all, nothing more than a warmup,” replied Nagumo. “I’m fine with getting people expelled, if I have to. That’s the way this school operates.”<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Congratulates him loudly; admits never wanting him expelled so they can keep facing each other; the trust discarded as game XP.<span class=\"pg\">p.229–237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tachibana Akane<\/b> Calls her over for the reveal; the target chosen over Manabu to watch his face.<span class=\"pg\">p.231–235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Fujimaki<\/b> Enigmatic wording draws Fujimaki’s stern face; then the “nothing to do with me” denial under the shout-down.<span class=\"pg\">p.229–232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishikura<\/b> Quiet Class B observer beside him; the collusion and the twenty-million advance read by the POV.<span class=\"pg\">p.229, 238–240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ikari Momoko<\/b> Her naming of Tachibana is the trap’s firing pin.<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Trap set without the school realizing it; Class B representative; large group held low; Nagumo paid twenty million private points up front so Class B would cooperate.<span class=\"pg\">p.232, 238–240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Effect<\/span> Forces the lifeline spend; keeps the A–B gap from widening while Class A burns cash; “warmup” for what comes next.<span class=\"pg\">p.236–240<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v8-p227-1\">← Before: Ch.9 half 1: second place with a smile<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v9-p7-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami horikita-manabu hoshinomiya-chie nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi vice presidential interview of ichinose student council room on a day off  vice president nagumo interviews first year class b ichinose honami one on one after president horikita rejected her application   1st year  class b  ichinose honami  huh  seeks her chiefly as personal property   class b like himself and outstanding grades are bonuses  the important question is whether she is worth keeping at his side   i hear you were on the student council  and student council president no less  during middle school   i heard from your homeroom teacher  hoshinomiya sensei  looks like your results on the entrance exams were also outstanding  lies that horikita rejected ichinose out of hand for not being class a and that the man obsesses over status   the narration states horikita assesses talent from d or a alike   it s because president horikita s a strict person  in all likelihood  he already rejected you out of hand because you re not in class a  claims he confessed the full truth behind his own class b assignment when applying to the council and that it resulted in his current position  refuses to say what that confession was   sorry but i have no intention of answering that  right now  the one being questioned is you  ichinose  presses why a student with her grades  interpersonal skills and middle school presidency is in class    there must be some reason for that   someone who is unable to grab hold of this opportunity has no place in the student council   it won t leave this room  of course  your secret is our secret  interviewer who extracts her secret under a promise of confidentiality while framing her as prospective personal property  slanders horikita s standards to ichinose  the narration marks the slander as a lie  obtains ichinose s entrance exam results from hoshinomiya sensei","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v9-p7-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Vice presidential interview of Ichinose<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.7–11<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Student council room on a day off; Vice President Nagumo interviews first-year Class B Ichinose Honami one-on-one after President Horikita rejected her application.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“1st year, Class B, Ichinose Honami, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.7<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I hear you were on the student council, and student council president no less, during middle school?”<span class=\"pg\">p.8<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I heard from your homeroom teacher, Hoshinomiya-sensei. Looks like your results on the entrance exams were also outstanding.”<span class=\"pg\">p.8<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Seeks her chiefly as personal property — Class B like himself and outstanding grades are bonuses; the important question is whether she is worth keeping at his side.<span class=\"pg\">p.8<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Lies that Horikita rejected Ichinose out of hand for not being Class A and that the man obsesses over status — the narration states Horikita assesses talent from D or A alike.<span class=\"pg\">p.9<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s because President Horikita’s a strict person. In all likelihood, he already rejected you out of hand because you’re not in Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.9<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Claims he confessed the full truth behind his own Class B assignment when applying to the council and that it resulted in his current position; refuses to say what that confession was.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry but I have no intention of answering that. Right now, the one being questioned is you, Ichinose.”<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Presses why a student with her grades, interpersonal skills and middle-school presidency is in Class — “There must be some reason for that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Someone who is unable to grab hold of this opportunity has no place in the student council.”<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It won’t leave this room, of course. Your secret is our secret.”<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Interviewer who extracts her secret under a promise of confidentiality while framing her as prospective personal property.<span class=\"pg\">p.7–11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Slanders Horikita’s standards to Ichinose; the narration marks the slander as a lie.<span class=\"pg\">p.9<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> Obtains Ichinose’s entrance-exam results from Hoshinomiya-sensei.<span class=\"pg\">p.8<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v9-p14-1\">→ After: Audience with Sakayanagi; Kōenji’s point loophole<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v9-p14-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"action spoken","w":"sakayanagi-arisu kouenji-rokusuke ryuuen-kakeru sudou-ken ishizaki-daichi ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-manabu nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi audience with sakayanagi  koenji s point loophole early february after the training camp  sakayanagi arisu visits the student council room  which nagumo has remade in his own formal style   did horikita senpai recommend you for the student council  by any chance   by showing me an appropriate amount of talent  that s the only way  first off  it s not too late to join the student council you know  come over to my side  sakayanagi   both you and ryuuen  we ve got a lot of interesting 1st years this year  don t we  mentions another  1st year  has an appointment to hurry sakayanagi  previously shared information with her about ichinose   i don t recall giving you permission to  go that far  sakayanagi   honami is my personal property i plan on loving  i only gave you permission to weaken her a bit   you re a bold woman  aren t you afraid of me  only authorized weakening of ichinose  not expulsion  treats the possibility of expulsion as beyond the permission he granted   very well  sakayanagi  the student council too will turn a blind eye to your actions  narration  not the least bit trustworthy  will throw away someone who could become an asset for the student council   unfortunately for you  i don t particularly dislike the use of violence either   unlike horikita senpai  i don t plan to crack down on them either  for the sudo ishizaki fight he would not push to expulsion   he would suspend the parties involved rather than hand down a harsher sentence than the previous president   koenji seems to be the only one in possession of an amount greater than what the school permits after all  it s a form of rule violation  private points are collected at graduation and worthless afterward  a third year may entrust them to an underclassman  he wants the 20 million point class a rule revised and says repeal would not apply to the first years  koenji s pre graduation purchases tipped the school off to a loophole   i definitely lost horikita senpai s trust and the trust of the students of 3rd year class a  deliberately threw away horikita senpai s trust during the training camp  narration  even breaking the rules established with horikita manabu had been planned from the beginning   ayanokoji  i am somewhat familiar with that name  he s a 1st year  is he not  ends the ayanokoji topic when sakayanagi says she does not know the name  refuses her offer to investigate him  receives her report on the planned ichinose attack  grants the council a blind eye  debates violence and point rules  and asks about ayanokoji  koenji s private points conversation at the training camp is the source sakayanagi reopens  nagumo treats koenji as the rule violating holder of excess points  names ryuuen with sakayanagi as an interesting first year who would not hesitate to make enemies of anyone  recalls the class d class c fight involving sudou and ishizaki s groups when asked how he would have sentenced it  same fight recollection   he would suspend rather than expel  asks sakayanagi about ayanokoji by name and then drops the subject  contrasts his own council posture with horikita senpai s  admits losing horikita senpai s trust  planned the break with manabu from the start","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v9-p14-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Audience with Sakayanagi; Kōenji’s point loophole<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.14–24<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Early February after the training camp; Sakayanagi Arisu visits the student council room, which Nagumo has remade in his own formal style.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+1 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Did Horikita-senpai recommend you for the student council, by any chance?”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“By showing me an appropriate amount of talent. That’s the only way. First off, it’s not too late to join the student council you know? Come over to my side, Sakayanagi.”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Both you and Ryuuen. We’ve got a lot of interesting 1st years this year, don’t we?”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>23 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Mentions another ‘1st year’ has an appointment to hurry Sakayanagi; previously shared information with her about Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t recall giving you permission to ‘go that far’, Sakayanagi.”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Honami is my personal property I plan on loving. I only gave you permission to weaken her a bit.”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re a bold woman. Aren’t you afraid of me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Only authorized weakening of Ichinose, not expulsion; treats the possibility of expulsion as beyond the permission he granted.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Very well, Sakayanagi. The student council too will turn a blind eye to your actions.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Narration: not the least bit trustworthy; will throw away someone who could become an asset for the student council.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unfortunately for you, I don’t particularly dislike the use of violence either.”<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unlike Horikita-senpai, I don’t plan to crack down on them either”<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> For the Sudō–Ishizaki fight he would not push to expulsion — he would suspend the parties involved rather than hand down a harsher sentence than the previous president.<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kōenji seems to be the only one in possession of an amount greater than what the school permits after all. It’s a form of rule violation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Private points are collected at graduation and worthless afterward; a third year may entrust them to an underclassman; he wants the 20-million-point Class A rule revised and says repeal would not apply to the first years; Kōenji’s pre-graduation purchases tipped the school off to a loophole.<span class=\"pg\">p.20–22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I definitely lost Horikita-senpai’s trust and the trust of the students of 3rd year Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Deliberately threw away Horikita-senpai’s trust during the training camp; narration: even breaking the rules established with Horikita Manabu had been planned from the beginning.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokōji…? I am somewhat familiar with that name. He’s a 1st year, is he not?”<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Ends the Ayanokōji topic when Sakayanagi says she does not know the name; refuses her offer to investigate him.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Receives her report on the planned Ichinose attack, grants the council a blind eye, debates violence and point rules, and asks about Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.14–24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Kōenji’s private-points conversation at the training camp is the source Sakayanagi reopens; Nagumo treats Kōenji as the rule-violating holder of excess points.<span class=\"pg\">p.20–21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Names Ryuuen with Sakayanagi as an interesting first year who would not hesitate to make enemies of anyone.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Recalls the Class D–Class C fight involving Sudou and Ishizaki’s groups when asked how he would have sentenced it.<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Same fight recollection — he would suspend rather than expel.<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Asks Sakayanagi about Ayanokōji by name and then drops the subject.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Contrasts his own council posture with Horikita-senpai’s; admits losing Horikita-senpai’s trust; planned the break with Manabu from the start.<span class=\"pg\">p.14, 19, 23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v9-p7-1\">← Before: Vice presidential interview of Ichinose<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v9-p100-1\">→ After: Named as Kushida’s new lever<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v9-p100-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"","w":"kushida-kikyou horikita-manabu nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi named as kushida s new lever she made contact with him asking for help expelling suzune  manabu s relationship with him deteriorated at the last training camp   he expects another move  does not appear  named in manabu s call only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v9-p100-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Named as Kushida’s new lever<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.100<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She made contact with him asking for help expelling Suzune.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Manabu’s relationship with him deteriorated at the last training camp — he expects another move.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Does not appear; named in Manabu’s call only.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v9-p14-1\">← Before: Audience with Sakayanagi; Kōenji’s point loophole<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v9-p120-1\">→ After: The remark that set the tail running<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v9-p120-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi horikita-manabu ayanokouji-kiyotaka nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi the remark that set the tail running his enigmatic claim   ayanokoji is somebody manabu holds in higher esteem than anyone   is what changed hashimoto s evaluation  the remark is framed as manabu s judgement  passed through the current president  the subject  hashimoto planned to pass it off as a joke and could not  does not appear  named through his remark only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v9-p120-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The remark that set the tail running<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.120<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> His enigmatic claim — Ayanokōji is somebody Manabu holds in higher esteem than anyone — is what changed Hashimoto’s evaluation.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> The remark is framed as Manabu’s judgement, passed through the current president.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The subject; Hashimoto planned to pass it off as a joke and could not.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Does not appear; named through his remark only.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v9-p100-1\">← Before: Named as Kushida’s new lever<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v9-p157-1\">→ After: Named at a distance<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v9-p157-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"","w":"nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi named at a distance named twice from a distance this chapter   as the president hashimoto invokes  and in the call as the risk to the elder horikita  hashimoto invokes the current student council president as someone who would turn a blind eye to petty disputes   his grounds for throwing the first kick  in the call  his influence over all of the second years could be lent to the third year class b  and he goes for weak points that are easy to exploit   as with targeting tachibana akane during the training camp","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v9-p157-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Named at a distance<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.157, 165<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named twice from a distance this chapter — as the president Hashimoto invokes, and in the call as the risk to the elder Horikita.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Hashimoto invokes the current student council president as someone who would turn a blind eye to petty disputes — his grounds for throwing the first kick.<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> In the call: his influence over all of the second-years could be lent to the third-year Class B, and he goes for weak points that are easy to exploit — as with targeting Tachibana Akane during the training camp.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v9-p120-1\">← Before: The remark that set the tail running<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v9-p180-1\">→ After: The school’s intervention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v9-p180-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi the school s intervention enters class b with hoshinomiya and chabashira  announces the school will punish rumor spreading   you re correct  this dispute does only involve the first years  however  as of today  it is against the rules to spread irresponsible rumors  intervenes to stop the rumors against her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v9-p180-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The school’s intervention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.180<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Enters Class B with Hoshinomiya and Chabashira; announces the school will punish rumor-spreading.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’re correct. This dispute does only involve the first-years. However, as of today, it is against the rules to spread irresponsible rumors.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Intervenes to stop the rumors against her.<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v9-p157-1\">← Before: Named at a distance<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v9-p218-1\">→ After: The encounter on exam day<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v9-p218-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi the encounter on exam day ichinose catches up to nagumo on the morning of the end of year exam and thanks him for recruiting her to the student council   don t you resent me  honami  looks at ayanokoji with displeasure  knowing he interfered  she thanks him  he is displeased with ayanokoji s interference","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v9-p218-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The encounter on exam day<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.218<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ichinose catches up to Nagumo on the morning of the end-of-year exam and thanks him for recruiting her to the student council. Looks at Ayanokōji with displeasure, knowing he interfered.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Don’t you resent me, Honami?”<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> She thanks him; he is displeased with Ayanokōji’s interference.<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v9-p180-1\">← Before: The school’s intervention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v10-p12-1","v":"y1v10","y":1,"o":12,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-manabu horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 1  exam results and the hallway encounter nagumo and manabu are seen talking in the hallway  nagumo spots ayanokoji  nagumo tests ayanokoji about the forum rumors  manabu backs ayanokoji up   in order to divert attention away from the slander that had been going around about ichinose honami  it seems that someone went and posted a bunch of rumors about various first year students on the school forums  nagumo invites horikita suzune to the student council  she rejects   if it s my senpai s little sister  i can have her take over as the student council president after i graduate  nagumo tells manabu to cherish time with his sister  manabu leaves   i would cherish the time i have left with my little sister if i were you  nagumo says taking down manabu is his only objective   of course  taking down horikita senpai is the only objective i have left at this school  nagumo competes with manabu  says taking him down is his only objective  invites her to the student council  she rejects  tests ayanokoji about forum rumors  spots ayanokoji and waves at him  preventing him from slipping away   yo ayanokoji  did you manage to pass the end of term exam   how cold  i don t think that s the right attitude to have when the student council president is right in front of you   well  whatever  you ve come by at just the right time  there s something i ve been wanting to ask you   so  what have you two celebrities been talking about   just having a little discussion with horikita senpai  ain t that right   tomorrow  a step ahead of the other school years  the third year students will begin a decisive battle that will determine whether horikita senpai will successfully graduate from class a or not  so i wanted to hear about it from him personally  are you interested too   how cold  you re acting like that just because you re horikita senpai s favorite  aren t you   don t delude yourself  ayanokoji  all that preferential treatment doesn t make you special  you just got lucky with the environment you were placed in  that s right  it s all thanks to that watchful  anxious classmate of yours right over there   come here   well  not exactly  but close enough  you re horikita senpai s little sister  right   i didn t expect my predecessor s little sister to get placed in class d after enrollment  i was surprised   i just wanted to meet with you and your little sister   concession  certainly not  do you really think that i d ever make a move on her  such a cute underclassman and moreover my senpai s precious little sister   even so  you don t have to be so distant do you  if only you had told me about your sister earlier  if you had  i would ve been able to invite her to the student council much sooner   this meeting is just for introductions  i ll invite you again another day   good grief  of course this isn t enough to get him to take me seriously   i would cherish the time i have left with my little sister if i were you   is it really so important for you to compete with the former president like this   well  what i do will depend on the details of the exam and horikita senpai himself   will there be any problems with next week s special exam on your end  president nagumo  i wouldn t expect the second years to have it easy either   well  i wonder  just carry on  hoping for my inevitable failure","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v10-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.1: Exam results and the hallway encounter<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V10 · p.12–29<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Nagumo and Manabu are seen talking in the hallway; Nagumo spots Ayanokōji. Nagumo tests Ayanokōji about the forum rumors; Manabu backs Ayanokōji up. Nagumo invites Horikita Suzune to the student council; she rejects. Nagumo tells Manabu to cherish time with his sister; Manabu leaves. Nagumo says taking down Manabu is his only objective.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“In order to divert attention away from the slander that had been going around about Ichinose Honami, it seems that someone went and posted a bunch of rumors about various first-year students on the school forums.”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“If it’s my senpai’s little sister, I can have her take over as the student council president after I graduate.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I would cherish the time I have left with my little sister if I were you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>26 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course. Taking down Horikita-senpai is the only objective I have left at this school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Nagumo competes with Manabu; says taking him down is his only objective.<span class=\"pg\">p.14–21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Invites her to the student council; she rejects.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Tests Ayanokōji about forum rumors.<span class=\"pg\">p.14–15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Spots Ayanokōji and waves at him, preventing him from slipping away.<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yo Ayanokōji. Did you manage to pass the end-of-term exam?”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How cold. I don’t think that’s the right attitude to have when the student council president is right in front of you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, whatever. You’ve come by at just the right time. There’s something I’ve been wanting to ask you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, what have you two celebrities been talking about?”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Just having a little discussion with Horikita-senpai. Ain’t that right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Tomorrow, a step ahead of the other school years, the third-year students will begin a decisive battle that will determine whether Horikita-senpai will successfully graduate from Class A or not. So I wanted to hear about it from him personally. Are you interested too?”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How cold. You’re acting like that just because you’re Horikita-senpai’s favorite, aren’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t delude yourself, Ayanokōji. All that preferential treatment doesn’t make you special. You just got lucky with the environment you were placed in. That’s right… It’s all thanks to that watchful, anxious classmate of yours right over there.”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Come here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, not exactly, but close enough. You’re Horikita-senpai’s little sister, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I didn’t expect my predecessor’s little sister to get placed in Class D after enrollment. I was surprised.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I just wanted to meet with you and your little sister.”<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Concession? Certainly not! Do you really think that I’d ever make a move on her? Such a cute underclassman and moreover my senpai’s precious little sister?”<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even so, you don’t have to be so distant do you? If only you had told me about your sister earlier. If you had, I would’ve been able to invite her to the student council much sooner.”<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This meeting is just for introductions. I’ll invite you again another day.”<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Good grief. Of course this isn’t enough to get him to take me seriously.”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I would cherish the time I have left with my little sister if I were you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is it really so important for you to compete with the former president like this?”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, what I do will depend on the details of the exam and Horikita-senpai himself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Will there be any problems with next week’s special exam on your end, president Nagumo? I wouldn’t expect the second-years to have it easy either.”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I wonder. Just carry on, hoping for my inevitable failure.”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v10-p97-1\">→ After: Ch.3: Ichinose’s deal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v10-p97-1","v":"y1v10","y":1,"o":12,"k":"","w":"nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 3  ichinose s deal asahina reveals ichinose asked nagumo for points and he consented  nagumo s condition for lending points is a relationship with ichinose  nagumo does not appear in person  his actions are reported by asahina","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v10-p97-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: Ichinose’s deal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V10 · p.97–103<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Asahina reveals Ichinose asked Nagumo for points and he consented. Nagumo’s condition for lending points is a relationship with Ichinose.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Nagumo does not appear in person; his actions are reported by Asahina.<span class=\"pg\">p.99–101<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v10-p12-1\">← Before: Ch.1: Exam results and the hallway encounter<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v10-p165-1\">→ After: Ch.4: Third-year politics<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v10-p165-1","v":"y1v10","y":1,"o":12,"k":"","w":"nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 4  third year politics tachibana reports nagumo has been in close contact with third year class b recently  nagumo does not appear in person  his moves are discussed at the meeting","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v10-p165-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: Third-year politics<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V10 · p.165–166<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Tachibana reports Nagumo has been in close contact with third-year Class B recently.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Nagumo does not appear in person; his moves are discussed at the meeting.<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v10-p97-1\">← Before: Ch.3: Ichinose’s deal<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v10-p257-1\">→ After: Ch.6: Lending points to Ichinose<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v10-p257-1","v":"y1v10","y":1,"o":12,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 6  lending points to ichinose takes ichinose s call and confirms their arrangement   honami  this is about our little arrangement  right  asks how many more points she needs after she collects her classmates  points   how many more do you need  answers without hesitation when ichinose asks whether he likes her   i wouldn t have made this a condition if i didn t like you  warns her about his deadline before transferring the points   be careful  i m a man who s fussy about keeping deadlines  confirms the conditions and pressures her to decide","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v10-p257-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: Lending points to Ichinose<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V10 · p.257–259<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Takes Ichinose’s call and confirms their arrangement. Asks how many more points she needs after she collects her classmates’ points. Answers without hesitation when Ichinose asks whether he likes her. Warns her about his deadline before transferring the points.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Honami? This is about our little arrangement, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“How many more do you need?”<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I wouldn’t have made this a condition if I didn’t like you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.259<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Be careful. I’m a man who’s fussy about keeping deadlines.”<span class=\"pg\">p.259<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Confirms the conditions and pressures her to decide.<span class=\"pg\">p.257–259<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v10-p165-1\">← Before: Ch.4: Third-year politics<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v11_5-p94-1","v":"y1v11.5","y":1,"o":14,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-manabu horikita-suzune asahina-nazuna kiriyama-ikuto ayanokouji-kiyotaka nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 1  graduation farewells as current student council president  nagumo approaches horikita manabu after the graduates  meeting and congratulates him on graduating   congratulations on graduating  horikita senpai  he tells manabu he was unable to threaten him  attributing it in part to being in a different year  nagumo shakes manabu s hand and exchanges words with him about the past year  he declares he will use his remaining year to turn the school into a meritocracy based on ability  after parting from manabu  nagumo approaches horikita suzune and speaks to her as manabu s sister  in conversation with asahina and others  nagumo maintains that he did not lose to horikita manabu despite manabu graduating from class a  congratulates him and exchanges parting words as successor and graduate  approaches and speaks to her during the farewells  is accompanied by her and discusses the outcome with her  appears with him among student council members at the farewell  is observed by him during the farewell exchanges","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v11_5-p94-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.1: Graduation farewells<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11.5 · p.94–104<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">As current student council president, Nagumo approaches Horikita Manabu after the graduates’ meeting and congratulates him on graduating. He tells Manabu he was unable to threaten him, attributing it in part to being in a different year. Nagumo shakes Manabu’s hand and exchanges words with him about the past year. He declares he will use his remaining year to turn the school into a meritocracy based on ability. After parting from Manabu, Nagumo approaches Horikita Suzune and speaks to her as Manabu’s sister. In conversation with Asahina and others, Nagumo maintains that he did not lose to Horikita Manabu despite Manabu graduating from Class A.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"asahina-nazuna.html\">Asahina Nazuna<\/a> · <a href=\"kiriyama-ikuto.html\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Congratulations on graduating, Horikita-senpai.”<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Congratulates him and exchanges parting words as successor and graduate.<span class=\"pg\">p.94–98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Approaches and speaks to her during the farewells.<span class=\"pg\">p.98–104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Asahina Nazuna<\/b> Is accompanied by her and discusses the outcome with her.<span class=\"pg\">p.94–104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> Appears with him among student council members at the farewell.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Is observed by him during the farewell exchanges.<span class=\"pg\">p.94–104<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v1-p35-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"","w":"nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi nagumo mentioned in passing named in the context of the student council  named in the context of tsukishiro s actions  named in the context of the student council room  passing mentions  not a distinct scene presence  passing mention only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v1-p35-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Nagumo mentioned in passing<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.35–36, 40, 317–318<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the context of the student council. Named in the context of Tsukishiro&#x27;s actions. Named in the context of the student council room.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mentions; not a distinct scene presence.<span class=\"pg\">p.35–36, 40, 317–318<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only.<span class=\"pg\">p.35–36, 40, 317–318<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v2-p75-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi nagumo accepts horikita and challenges ayanokoji he accepts horikita into the student council with a condition  warning her that past presidents graduated in class a  he invites ayanokoji to join too  declined   well  what a turn of events  i don t really want to obediently say yes  he tells ayanokoji to look forward to playing together in summer  then probes kiriyama about why he attended   i ll play with you  so look forward to it  calculating and playful   he tests both horikita and ayanokoji while keeping kiriyama off balance  accepts her into the council  challenges him directly","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v2-p75-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Nagumo accepts Horikita and challenges Ayanokōji<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.75–82<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He accepts Horikita into the student council with a condition, warning her that past presidents graduated in Class A; he invites Ayanokōji to join too (declined). He tells Ayanokōji to look forward to playing together in summer, then probes Kiriyama about why he attended.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Well, what a turn of events! I don&#x27;t really want to obediently say yes.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;ll play with you, so look forward to it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calculating and playful — he tests both Horikita and Ayanokōji while keeping Kiriyama off balance.<span class=\"pg\">p.75–82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Accepts her into the council.<span class=\"pg\">p.75–78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Challenges him directly.<span class=\"pg\">p.79–82<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v2-p75-2\">→ After: Nagumo admits Horikita; challenges Ayanokōji<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v2-p75-2","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-manabu kiriyama nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi nagumo admits horikita  challenges ayanokoji in the student council office  receives horikita and ayanokoji  welcomes the conversation but invites her straight to the point   so what did you want to talk to me about  you didn t come just to talk  right   well  what a turn of events  i don t really want to obediently say yes   in other words  can i assume that you have the intention to become the student council president   she doesn t look that similar to him  but she really is horikita senpai s little sister   welcome to the student council  from today onward  i want you to work for me as a member of the council without any worries  suzune   then show me that isn t just all talk   are you going to join the student council by the way  ayanokouji   i knew you would say that   i ll play with you  so look forward to it   sakayanagi  ichinose  ryuuen  those people would probably cry from the joy  meritocratic and open  admits anyone to the council regardless of reason  unlike manabu  with a sharp eye for lies   sees through horikita s half truths but values her ambition  after she joins  pivots to ayanokoji  inviting him then declaring he ll  play  with him over summer    an order from the strong to the weak  questions her closely  welcomes her to the council  calls her  suzune  and motivates her to aim for class a  invites him to the council  he declines  then issues a veiled challenge  horikita s brother  whose traditions he replaced with reforms  his vice president  who reacts with surprise at his invitation to ayanokoji","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v2-p75-2\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Nagumo admits Horikita; challenges Ayanokōji<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.75–81<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In the student council office, receives Horikita and Ayanokōji; welcomes the conversation but invites her straight to the point.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"kiriyama.html\">Kiriyama<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;So what did you want to talk to me about? You didn&#x27;t come just to talk, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Well, what a turn of events! I don&#x27;t really want to obediently say yes.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;In other words, can I assume that you have the intention to become the student council president?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;She doesn&#x27;t look that similar to him, but she really is Horikita-senpai&#x27;s little sister!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Welcome to the student council. From today onward, I want you to work for me as a member of the council without any worries, Suzune.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Then show me that isn&#x27;t just all talk.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Are you going to join the student council by the way? Ayanokouji.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I knew you would say that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;ll play with you, so look forward to it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sakayanagi, Ichinose, Ryuuen. Those people would probably cry from the joy.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Meritocratic and open (admits anyone to the council regardless of reason, unlike Manabu), with a sharp eye for lies — sees through Horikita&#x27;s half-truths but values her ambition; after she joins, pivots to Ayanokōji, inviting him then declaring he&#x27;ll &quot;play&quot; with him over summer — &quot;an order from the strong to the weak.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.75–81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Questions her closely, welcomes her to the council, calls her &quot;Suzune,&quot; and motivates her to aim for Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.75–80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Invites him to the council (he declines), then issues a veiled challenge.<span class=\"pg\">p.80–81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Horikita&#x27;s brother, whose traditions he replaced with reforms.<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama<\/b> His vice president, who reacts with surprise at his invitation to Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.78, 80<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v2-p75-1\">← Before: Nagumo accepts Horikita and challenges Ayanokōji<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v3-p130-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka asahina-nazuna horikita-suzune masuwaka nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi nagumo s beach warning and hidden strategy in the ocean near the task site with asahina and other third years  having rented swimsuits and a beach ball  beckons ayanokoji over   i ll say it again just to be sure  don t get in my way  got it   how about you come take a swim with us   the real event starts tomorrow   first and second years have no right to stand on the winners  podium  you re no exception either  so keep that in mind   horikita senpai would probably be fairly disappointed if you self destructed and got yourself expelled   in that case  you d better group up with someone as soon as possible  confident and calculating   plays relaxed on the beach while hiding a strategy to keep first second years off the podium  to be used if they threaten the top  warns ayanokoji pointedly  references horikita  and walks off with masuwaka to discuss something privately  away from ayanokoji  warns him not to get in his way  hints he has a strategy against lower years   ayanokoji suspects it s real  class 2 c s mii chan playing in the ocean  tries to warn ayanokoji about nagumo  references her   knows of their connection  third year who calls nagumo away for a private talk","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v3-p130-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Nagumo&#x27;s beach warning and hidden strategy<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.130–132<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In the ocean near the Task site with Asahina and other third-years, having rented swimsuits and a beach ball; beckons Ayanokōji over.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"asahina-nazuna.html\">Asahina Nazuna<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#masuwaka\">Masuwaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;ll say it again just to be sure: Don&#x27;t get in my way, got it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;How about you come take a swim with us?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;the real event starts tomorrow.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;First and second-years have no right to stand on the winners&#x27; podium. You&#x27;re no exception either, so keep that in mind.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Horikita-senpai would probably be fairly disappointed if you self-destructed and got yourself expelled.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;In that case, you&#x27;d better group up with someone as soon as possible.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Confident and calculating — plays relaxed on the beach while hiding a strategy to keep first/second-years off the podium (to be used if they threaten the top); warns Ayanokōji pointedly, references Horikita, and walks off with Masuwaka to discuss something privately (away from Ayanokōji).<span class=\"pg\">p.130–132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Warns him not to get in his way; hints he has a strategy against lower years — Ayanokōji suspects it&#x27;s real.<span class=\"pg\">p.130–132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Asahina Nazuna<\/b> Class 2-C&#x27;s Mii-chan playing in the ocean; tries to warn Ayanokōji about Nagumo.<span class=\"pg\">p.131–132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> References her — knows of their connection.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Masuwaka<\/b> Third-year who calls Nagumo away for a private talk.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v3-p130-2\">→ After: Nagumo appears at the Beach Flags Task<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v3-p130-2","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"","w":"nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi nagumo appears at the beach flags task he appears at the beach flags task and talks with ayanokoji  he suggests ayanokoji should group up with someone  calculating and observant","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v3-p130-2\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Nagumo appears at the Beach Flags Task<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.130–132<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He appears at the Beach Flags Task and talks with Ayanokōji; he suggests Ayanokōji should group up with someone.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calculating and observant.<span class=\"pg\">p.130–132<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v3-p130-1\">← Before: Nagumo&#x27;s beach warning and hidden strategy<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v4-p10-1","v":"y2v4","y":2,"o":19,"k":"","w":"nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi nagumo mentioned in passing named in the context of the exam  named in the context of the student council  named in the context of tsukishiro s actions  passing mentions  not a distinct scene presence  passing mention only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v4-p10-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Nagumo mentioned in passing<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4 · p.10–37<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the context of the exam. Named in the context of the student council. Named in the context of Tsukishiro&#x27;s actions.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mentions; not a distinct scene presence.<span class=\"pg\">p.10–37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only.<span class=\"pg\">p.10–37<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v4_5-p10-1","v":"y2v4.5","y":2,"o":20,"k":"","w":"nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi nagumo miyabi mentioned in passing named in this volume  passing mentions on pages  p 23 24  p 37 38  p 41 43  p 45 54  p 87  passing mention only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v4_5-p10-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">nagumo-miyabi mentioned in passing<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4.5 · p.10-290<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in this volume.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mentions on pages: p.23-24, p.37-38, p.41-43, p.45-54, p.87.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v5-p7-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"","w":"nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi nagumo miyabi mentioned in passing named in this volume  passing mentions on pages  p 241 242  passing mention only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v5-p7-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">nagumo-miyabi mentioned in passing<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.7-243<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in this volume.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mentions on pages: p.241-242.<span class=\"pg\">p.7<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only.<span class=\"pg\">p.7<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v6-p50-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ichinose-honami nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi nagumo s challenge  lunch with ichinose  yo  ayanokouji  anything unusual happen in your daily life lately   as the student council president  you can talk to me about those worries  you know   you ve already heard the rules for the sports festival  right  it means the time when we can settle our score has come  ayanokouji   if you beat me in even one head to head match during this sports festival  everything that s happened between us will be water under the bridge   you ll participate in all five competitions i specify   well  that s all you can say for now  i ll give you one week   lately  i ve been having lunch together with honami in the student council room every day  arrogant and calculating   sees through ayanokoji s feigned modesty  demands five head to head sports events  one loss   truce  to force a direct defeat  and stages a humiliating lunch with ichinose  whom he s been meeting daily  to display his control  he controls the entire third year  and his attachment to ichinose  possibly because of ayanokoji  may end with her if she fails  his obsession   wants a direct defeat  ayanokoji sees through his strategy  eats lunch with her daily and confides  ayanokoji wonders if his attachment is real or a ploy","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v6-p50-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Nagumo&#x27;s challenge; lunch with Ichinose<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.50–57<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Yo, Ayanokouji. Anything unusual happen in your daily life lately?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;As the student council president, you can talk to me about those worries, you know?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You&#x27;ve already heard the rules for the Sports Festival, right? It means the time when we can settle our score has come, Ayanokouji.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;if you beat me in even one head-to-head match during this sports festival, everything that&#x27;s happened between us will be water under the bridge.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You&#x27;ll participate in all five competitions I specify.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, that&#x27;s all you can say for now. I&#x27;ll give you one week.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Lately, I&#x27;ve been having lunch together with Honami in the student council room every day.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Arrogant and calculating — sees through Ayanokōji&#x27;s feigned modesty, demands five head-to-head sports events (one loss = truce) to force a direct defeat, and stages a humiliating lunch with Ichinose (whom he&#x27;s been meeting daily) to display his control; he controls the entire third year, and his attachment to Ichinose (possibly because of Ayanokōji) may end with her if she fails.<span class=\"pg\">p.50–58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> His obsession — wants a direct defeat; Ayanokōji sees through his strategy.<span class=\"pg\">p.50–58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Eats lunch with her daily and confides; Ayanokōji wonders if his attachment is real or a ploy.<span class=\"pg\">p.53–57<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v6-p241-1\">→ After: Nagumo: five wins, no joy, and Ayanokōji&#x27;s absence<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v6-p241-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kiryuin-fuuka horikita-suzune nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi nagumo  five wins  no joy  and ayanokoji s absence delivers the opening speech boldly before the guests  political figures tied to the school   in no way inferior  to horikita manabu s example   don t make me laugh  as if winning a competition of that level would mean anything to me   don t worry  kiryuuin  you don t need to tell me  i m not going to play around with ayanokouji anymore  he chose not to fight me  wins five consecutive events but stays expressionless  he s guaranteed class a regardless  kiryuin needles him that he could have gathered all the weaklings for easy wins and that ayanokoji  ran away  from their fight  at lunch he tells horikita that ayanokoji bailing on him means someone else will pay the price  hinting at trouble for her grade  he wanted a direct fight  quench my thirst  ayanokoji s absence frustrates him  his fellow third year   she provokes him  they ve spoken more in the six months since ayanokoji s involvement than in two years  he invites her to lunch and presses about ayanokoji","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v6-p241-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Nagumo: five wins, no joy, and Ayanokōji&#x27;s absence<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.241–257<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Delivers the opening speech boldly before the guests (political figures tied to the school), &quot;in no way inferior&quot; to Horikita Manabu&#x27;s example.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"kiryuin-fuuka.html\">Kiryuin Fuuka<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Don&#x27;t make me laugh. As if winning a competition of that level would mean anything to me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Don&#x27;t worry, Kiryuuin. You don&#x27;t need to tell me; I&#x27;m not going to play around with Ayanokouji anymore. He chose not to fight me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Wins five consecutive events but stays expressionless (he&#x27;s guaranteed Class A regardless); Kiryūin needles him that he could have gathered all the weaklings for easy wins and that Ayanokōji &quot;ran away&quot; from their fight; at lunch he tells Horikita that Ayanokōji bailing on him means someone else will pay the price, hinting at trouble for her grade.<span class=\"pg\">p.250–257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He wanted a direct fight (&quot;quench my thirst&quot;); Ayanokōji&#x27;s absence frustrates him.<span class=\"pg\">p.252–257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiryuin Fuuka<\/b> His fellow third-year — she provokes him; they&#x27;ve spoken more in the six months since Ayanokōji&#x27;s involvement than in two years.<span class=\"pg\">p.251–253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> He invites her to lunch and presses about Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.255–257<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v6-p50-1\">← Before: Nagumo&#x27;s challenge; lunch with Ichinose<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v7-p44-1","v":"y2v7","y":2,"o":23,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi nagumo  loses his  game  to ayanokoji s sincerity  the game with you is over and so is my school life  as a result  i don t give a shit about the cultural festival   you ran away from the last chance i gave you at the sports festival   understand this  ayanokoji  i m allowed to challenge you to a fight  but you re not allowed to challenge me to a fight   you have loose screws  ayanokoji  belligerent but bored   he s lost interest in the festival  his  game  with ayanokoji over  dismisses ryuen s 5 million bet  but is drawn into ayanokoji s proposal  when ayanokoji genuinely says  it doesn t matter who it is   even kei  and refuses to fight back no matter who he expels  nagumo s smile vanishes   he concedes  i have no choice but to accept your current proposal  agreeing to a future match  but leaves unsettled  loose screws  calling ayanokoji crazy  he accepts the match and the favor  but ayanokoji s cold sincerity about kei rattles him  he threatens kei to sway ayanokoji   it fails","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v7-p44-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Nagumo: loses his &quot;game&quot; to Ayanokōji&#x27;s sincerity<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V7 · p.44–53<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;the game with you is over and so is my school life. As a result, I don&#x27;t give a shit about the cultural festival.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You ran away from the last chance I gave you at the sports festival.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Understand this, Ayanokōji. I&#x27;m allowed to challenge you to a fight, but you&#x27;re not allowed to challenge me to a fight.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You have loose screws, Ayanokōji.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Belligerent but bored — he&#x27;s lost interest in the festival (his &quot;game&quot; with Ayanokōji over), dismisses Ryūen&#x27;s 5-million bet, but is drawn into Ayanokōji&#x27;s proposal; when Ayanokōji genuinely says &quot;it doesn&#x27;t matter who it is&quot; (even Kei) and refuses to fight back no matter who he expels, Nagumo&#x27;s smile vanishes — he concedes (&quot;I have no choice but to accept your current proposal&quot;), agreeing to a future match, but leaves unsettled (&quot;loose screws&quot;), calling Ayanokōji crazy.<span class=\"pg\">p.44–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He accepts the match and the favor, but Ayanokōji&#x27;s cold sincerity about Kei rattles him.<span class=\"pg\">p.44–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> He threatens Kei to sway Ayanokōji — it fails.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v8-p11-1","v":"y2v8","y":2,"o":24,"k":"","w":"nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi nagumo miyabi mentioned in passing named in this volume  passing mentions on pages  p 61  p 207  passing mention only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v8-p11-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">nagumo-miyabi mentioned in passing<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V8 · p.11-208<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in this volume.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mentions on pages: p.61, p.207.<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only.<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v9-p18-1","v":"y2v9","y":2,"o":25,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kiryuin-fuuka ichinose-honami nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi nagumo  his final act as president  exposed by kiryuin  if i win  i want to get some private points from you   i m sorry for interrupting  but i want to talk about what you said earlier    kiryuin  it was impossible to replace honami now   you re a student in suzune s class  please help me gather members for the student council  steps down as president  arranging an election between horikita and ichinose  with 1 3 of votes at his discretion  and betting 20 million points with ayanokoji   but kiryuin publicly exposes that he ordered first year yamanaka to shoplift as a  mission  he refuses to acknowledge it  no evidence  but ichinose s withdrawal ends his  match  he hands the presidency to an unopposed horikita  tasks her  and ayanokoji  with recruiting  and accepts hokkaido souvenirs    you re very disciplined in a strange way  he loses his 20 million point bet  ichinose withdrew  but still ropes him into helping recruit  she bursts in and exposes the shoplifting order   he tries to  make a pass  at her but she s unmoved   you are full of faults  but i appreciate what you said  he wanted her in the election  i don t get it    her withdrawal frustrates him  damn it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v9-p18-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Nagumo: his final act as president; exposed by Kiryūin<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V9 · p.18–38<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"kiryuin-fuuka.html\">Kiryuin Fuuka<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If I win, I want to get some private points from you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;m sorry for interrupting, but I want to talk about what you said earlier.&quot; — Kiryūin<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It was impossible to replace Honami now.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You&#x27;re a student in Suzune&#x27;s class. Please help me gather members for the student council.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Steps down as president, arranging an election between Horikita and Ichinose (with 1/3 of votes at his discretion) and betting 20 million points with Ayanokōji — but Kiryūin publicly exposes that he ordered first-year Yamanaka to shoplift as a &quot;mission&quot;; he refuses to acknowledge it (no evidence), but Ichinose&#x27;s withdrawal ends his &quot;match&quot;; he hands the presidency to an unopposed Horikita, tasks her (and Ayanokōji) with recruiting, and accepts Hokkaido souvenirs — &quot;You&#x27;re very disciplined in a strange way.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.18–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He loses his 20-million-point bet (Ichinose withdrew) but still ropes him into helping recruit.<span class=\"pg\">p.24–37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiryuin Fuuka<\/b> She bursts in and exposes the shoplifting order — he tries to &quot;make a pass&quot; at her but she&#x27;s unmoved; &quot;You are full of faults, but I appreciate what you said.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.29–33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> He wanted her in the election (&quot;I don&#x27;t get it&quot;) — her withdrawal frustrates him (&quot;Damn it…&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.33–35<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v9-p74-1\">→ After: Nagumo&#x27;s farewell: regrets at the handover<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v9-p74-1","v":"y2v9","y":2,"o":25,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi nagumo s farewell  regrets at the handover at the formal handover he pats the president s chair reluctantly  says the tenure was both long and short  and admits his regret   he wanted talented students to graduate in class a across class lines but could not overturn the school s decisions  he tells ayanokoji their battle is not over   well  i guess i m relieved of my duties as student council president now   it was both a long and short time  it s an indescribable feeling  reflective and slightly wistful at leaving   he acknowledges the limits of the council s power  takes pride in the oaa transfer ticket system he introduced  and hints at unfinished business with ayanokoji  hands her the presidency  she notes his influence on the school s rules  reminds him their battle is not over","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v9-p74-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Nagumo&#x27;s farewell: regrets at the handover<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V9 · p.74–75<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At the formal handover he pats the president&#x27;s chair reluctantly, says the tenure was both long and short, and admits his regret — he wanted talented students to graduate in Class A across class lines but could not overturn the school&#x27;s decisions; he tells Ayanokōji their battle is not over.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Well, I guess I&#x27;m relieved of my duties as student council president now.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It was both a long and short time. It&#x27;s an indescribable feeling.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reflective and slightly wistful at leaving — he acknowledges the limits of the council&#x27;s power, takes pride in the OAA/transfer-ticket system he introduced, and hints at unfinished business with Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.74–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Hands her the presidency; she notes his influence on the school&#x27;s rules.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Reminds him their battle is not over.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v9-p18-1\">← Before: Nagumo: his final act as president; exposed by Kiryūin<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v9_5-p49-1","v":"y2v9.5","y":2,"o":26,"k":"","w":"nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi nagumo mentioned in passing named in this volume  passing mention  locator pages  p 49  p 52  p 56  p 57  p 120  p 175  not line by line verified  substring false positives possible  not a scene presence  passing mention only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v9_5-p49-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Nagumo mentioned in passing<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V9.5 · p.49-175<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in this volume.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention (locator pages: p.49, p.52, p.56, p.57, p.120, p.175; not line-by-line verified; substring false positives possible). Not a scene presence.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v10-p9-1","v":"y2v10","y":2,"o":28,"k":"","w":"nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi nagumo miyabi mentioned in passing named in this volume  passing mention  locator pages  p 234  not line by line verified  substring false positives possible  not a scene presence  passing mention only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v10-p9-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">nagumo-miyabi mentioned in passing<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V10 · p.9-235<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in this volume.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention (locator pages: p.234; not line-by-line verified; substring false positives possible). Not a scene presence.<span class=\"pg\">p.9<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only.<span class=\"pg\">p.9<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v11-p11-1","v":"y2v11","y":2,"o":30,"k":"","w":"nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi nagumo miyabi mentioned in passing named in this volume  passing mention  locator pages  p 39  p 53 62  p 64 65  p 67 72  p 78  p 84  not line by line verified  substring false positives possible  not a scene presence  passing mention only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v11-p11-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">nagumo-miyabi mentioned in passing<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V11 · p.11-223<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in this volume.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention (locator pages: p.39, p.53-62, p.64-65, p.67-72, p.78, p.84; not line-by-line verified; substring false positives possible). Not a scene presence.<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Passing mention only.<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v11-p53-1\">→ After: Ch.2: The bet he sets before graduation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v11-p53-1","v":"y2v11","y":2,"o":30,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka asahina-nazuna kiryuin-fuuka horikita-suzune horikita-manabu nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 2  the bet he sets before graduation rest area  just before one  drooping of boredom with asahina  beckons kiyotaka over  asahina muscles into the sofa next to him   need  well  it s not much of a need  but i do have something to talk about   many of us third years are dealing with exams and job hunting at this time   do you want to know   i m going to university  i have no intention of using the class a privilege   that s one of the reasons i dominated the third year and became an overwhelming presence  whether i m in class b or class d at graduation  i believe i can get into the university i want and get a job at the company i desire with my own power   do you know why horikita suzune joined the student council  nazuna   this guy right here  ayanokoji was using suzune to keep an eye on me   horikita senpai did pass the baton to me  after all   i can assume you re willing to accept a match with me  right   actually  calling it a match is an exaggeration  it s more like a small bet   you participate in all the games  and when you lose three times  that s your defeat   yeah  even if kiryuin s group loses 19 times in a row  if you don t lose to anyone  it s a win   if i make being undefeated a condition and you lose in the first battle  it would be a real turn off  right   that s the way i like to treat you   nazuna seems to misunderstand  but victory or defeat is not determined solely by whether one is excellent  if the person on top isn t more capable  using a skilled person will only lead to their loss   ah  everything s going smoothly  it s going to be a match between me and ayanokoji as planned   huh  you ve really bought into ayanokoji  if you want  i can challenge you individually and not just in this exchange meeting  if we re both third years  there s no need to hold back  i ll even bet the ticket price for class a   she s just a woman  after all   you should also practice or something and prepare for the match   amasawa  from first year class a   she wasn t my pick  somehow  she heard rumors and knew about the next social gathering   sorry  but i don t like women who pretend to be cute or flatter me   i m leaving now  do your best  ayanokoji  his university choice  same one horikita manabu goes to  no need for the class a privilege  he dominated the third year on his own power  asahina is also bound for university but not the same level  terms  kiyotaka plays all 19 games  three individual losses end the bet  his group record irrelevant  nagumo demands his defeat  he smiles like he s already won  amasawa pressed herself onto his group  he recruited hesitantly  she heard the plans via yagami and tsukishiro  he sets the match inside the exchange meeting  he wants kiyotaka to lose in any game  he offers private points  nazuna sides with kiyotaka  she s irked by his  on top among the same sex  line  she hurt shoves him  he ignores it  kiryuin volunteered for the leader role to watch  he chalks it up to her usual cool distance  he believes kiyotaka used suzune to keep an eye on him when she joined the council  horikita manabu s university choice drew nagumo  the baton passed to nagumo as president","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v11-p53-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: The bet he sets before graduation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V11 · p.53–62<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Rest Area, just before one; drooping of boredom with Asahina; beckons Kiyotaka over; Asahina muscles into the sofa next to him.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"asahina-nazuna.html\">Asahina Nazuna<\/a> · <a href=\"kiryuin-fuuka.html\">Kiryuin Fuuka<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Need? Well, it&#x27;s not much of a need, but I do have something to talk about.”<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Many of us third-years are dealing with exams and job hunting at this time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Do you want to know?”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>28 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I&#x27;m going to university. I have no intention of using the Class A privilege.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s one of the reasons I dominated the third-year and became an overwhelming presence. Whether I&#x27;m in Class B or Class D at graduation, I believe I can get into the university I want and get a job at the company I desire with my own power.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you know why Horikita Suzune joined the student council, Nazuna?”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This guy right here. Ayanokōji was using Suzune to keep an eye on me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita-senpai did pass the baton to me, after all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can assume you&#x27;re willing to accept a match with me, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Actually, calling it a match is an exaggeration. It&#x27;s more like a small bet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You participate in all the games. And when you lose three times, that&#x27;s your defeat.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. Even if Kiryūin&#x27;s group loses 19 times in a row, if you don&#x27;t lose to anyone, it&#x27;s a win.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If I make being undefeated a condition and you lose in the first battle, it would be a real turn-off, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s the way I like to treat you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nazuna seems to misunderstand, but victory or defeat is not determined solely by whether one is excellent. If the person on top isn’t more capable, using a skilled person will only lead to their loss.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, everything&#x27;s going smoothly. It&#x27;s going to be a match between me and Ayanokōji as planned”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh, you&#x27;ve really bought into Ayanokōji. If you want, I can challenge you individually and not just in this exchange meeting. If we&#x27;re both third-years, there&#x27;s no need to hold back. I&#x27;ll even bet the ticket price for Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She&#x27;s just a woman, after all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You should also practice or something and prepare for the match.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Amasawa. From first-year Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She wasn&#x27;t my pick. Somehow, she heard rumors and knew about the next social gathering.”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry, but I don&#x27;t like women who pretend to be cute or flatter me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I&#x27;m leaving now. Do your best, Ayanokōji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His university choice: same one Horikita Manabu goes to; no need for the Class A privilege; he dominated the third-year on his own power; Asahina is also bound for university but not the same level.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Terms: Kiyotaka plays all 19 games; three individual losses end the bet; his group record irrelevant; Nagumo demands his defeat; he smiles like he&#x27;s already won.<span class=\"pg\">p.58–59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Amasawa pressed herself onto his group; he recruited hesitantly; she heard the plans via Yagami and Tsukishiro.<span class=\"pg\">p.62–65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He sets the match inside the exchange meeting; he wants Kiyotaka to lose in any game; he offers private points.<span class=\"pg\">p.53–66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Asahina Nazuna<\/b> Nazuna sides with Kiyotaka; she&#x27;s irked by his &quot;on top among the same sex&quot; line; she hurt-shoves him; he ignores it.<span class=\"pg\">p.53–64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiryuin Fuuka<\/b> Kiryūin volunteered for the leader role to watch; he chalks it up to her usual cool distance.<span class=\"pg\">p.60–62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> He believes Kiyotaka used Suzune to keep an eye on him when she joined the council.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Horikita Manabu&#x27;s university choice drew Nagumo; the baton passed to Nagumo as president.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–57<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v11-p11-1\">← Before: nagumo-miyabi mentioned in passing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v12-p20-1","v":"y2v12","y":2,"o":31,"k":"","w":"nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 1 3  mentioned named during ayanokoji s private reckoning about the balance of the four classes  p 20   both horikita manabu s and nagumo miyabi s classes had created a dominating system as a result  p 40  amasawa recounts her own near expulsion over the nagumo incident at the camp  p 50 51  recalled as the transfer fee discussion with hashimoto  the 20 million point transfer cost  and as the source of a 3 million private point reward for the camp bet  p 63  kiryuin reports that nagumo asked her to look into how ayanokoji would handle the special exam  he has no intention of seeing ayanokoji anymore  named throughout but never on page  not present  discussed only in others  speech and ayanokoji s thoughts","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v12-p20-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.1–3: Mentioned<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V12 · p.20, p.40, p.42, p.50–51, p.63<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named during Ayanokōji&#x27;s private reckoning about the balance of the four classes.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> p.20: &quot;Both Horikita Manabu&#x27;s and Nagumo Miyabi&#x27;s classes had created a dominating system as a result.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> p.40: Amasawa recounts her own near-expulsion over the Nagumo incident at the camp.<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> p.50–51: recalled as the transfer-fee discussion with Hashimoto (the 20 million point transfer cost) and as the source of a 3 million private-point reward for the camp bet.<span class=\"pg\">p.50–51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> p.63: Kiryūin reports that Nagumo asked her to look into how Ayanokōji would handle the special exam; he has no intention of seeing Ayanokōji anymore.<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Named throughout but never on-page; not present; discussed only in others&#x27; speech and Ayanokōji&#x27;s thoughts.<span class=\"pg\">p.20, p.40, p.42, p.50–51, p.63<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v12_5-p213-1","v":"y2v12.5","y":2,"o":32,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi epilogue mentioned appears in epilogue  appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y2v12_5-p213-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Epilogue<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V12.5 · p.213-216<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Mentioned/appears in Epilogue.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Appears in this volume.<span class=\"pg\">p.213-216<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"}];
